{"title":"2022 SSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95ec2e34502754f215bf68cdfe5c4088d44208d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\sum_{k=5}^{\\infty}2^{-10k}\\binom{2k}{10}.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"53\" /> Then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find the largest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d349d35077aa2c0c2cff4d09ad4cb05d56ade46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a\\mid mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e80cb6205d2e47608de59c7b66d9ff92fb50a3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{2k}{10} = \\left[y^{10}\\right](1+y)^{2k}.\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"53\" /> Substituting, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9add5428413075d89733abfae0c9152632b33184.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\left[y^{10}\\right]\\sum_{k=5}^{\\infty}2^{-10k}(y+1)^{2k}=\\left[y^{10}\\right]\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-10k}(y+1)^{2k}.\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"48\" /> We have  \\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}2^{-10k}(y+1)^{2k}&amp;=\\frac{1}{1-2^{-10}(y+1)^2}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{y+1}{32}}+\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{y+1}{32}}\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\sum_{k\\geq0}\\left(\\frac{y+1}{32}\\right)^k+\\sum_{k\\geq0}\\left(-\\frac{y+1}{32}\\right)^k\\right). \\end{align*} The coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb2b080e28bf22191584d4b8d20a6187c8f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{10}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> is \\begin{align*} S&amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\sum\\binom{k}{10}\\left(\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^k+\\sum\\binom{k}{10}\\left(-\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^k\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^{10}}{\\left(1-\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^{11}}+\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^{10}}{\\left(1+\\frac{1}{32}\\right)^{11}}\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{32}{31^{11}}+\\frac{32}{33^{11}}\\right)=\\frac{16(33^{11}+31^{11})}{(31\\cdot33)^11} \\end{align*} We can lift the exponent to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679aa9ec1491d68e4986f59a5d320566ba95819a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(33^{11}+31^{11})=v_2(33+31)+v_2(11) = 6,\\]\" width=\"338\" height=\"20\" /> giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f8576603098962a0fc152c4ef54ccd0c784af7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(16)+v_2(33^{11}+31^{11})=4+6=\\boxed{10}.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018021930\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2246/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26200:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018021930 and revision id 280154. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}